2026-11-06T02:57:03.0452986Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0461961Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0462617Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0463245Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0463515Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0463746Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0464091Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0464424Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0464978Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0465289Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0465496Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0466004Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0466242Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0466520Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:57:03.0467065Z   $ sh ./install-nix
